{"skill":{"slug":"eastmoney-stock-simulator","displayName":"eastmoney skills"},"version":{"version":"1.0.4","createdAt":1773890582881,"changelog":"eastmoney-stock-simulator 1.0.4 Changelog\n\n- Added primary_credential field for clearer credential configuration.\n- No changes to code or functional logic—metadata update only.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":21223,"sha256":"c1dee1a9a9814628dedd898b00234090da464d197fa57711e181b40a1fd12c0d","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/mx_stock_simulator.py","size":14100,"sha256":"c7aecb3a5837106eaa4ac25ad7ffb0cf2141888af3857a19f0cffe86e0d9c40e","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"scripts/requirements.txt","size":9,"sha256":"7cc4959877dbe6b6c63a8eb1bfe3bfb545fa8fe5b28b1b2c13e4a7c1c0d1c4d4","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2660,"sha256":"fc4f06385dbafc7028f6da9e0e7703ddf8c333db00b4c5845a4dc8037131c3fc","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789192726278,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a0a02694788266de5797199d0011ce6fcb21a8b65cb13595a760ddfc6ca13ca3","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a0a02694788266de5797199d0011ce6fcb21a8b65cb13595a760ddfc6ca13ca3","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780089969094},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":14,"checkedAt":1789192726278},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill fits a simulated stock-trading purpose, but it needs Review because it can submit or cancel simulated trades and send the API key to a configurable URL without enough safeguards.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill requires MX_APIKEY and uses MX_API_URL for outbound authenticated POST requests, but the implementation does not validate or restrict that URL before sending the API key and account payloads.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No hidden installer, remote payload, tool hijacking, or system persistence was found; the only dependency is requests, but it is unpinned.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifacts disclose trading and cancellation features, but they do not require a confirmation or dry-run before state-changing actions parsed from natural language.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill discloses automatic output files, and the script writes formatted and raw JSON account/trading responses to a fixed /root/.openclaw workspace path without explicit file permissions, retention, redaction, or opt-in controls.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is coherent for a simulated A-share portfolio skill, but the implemented script performs account-changing buy, sell, and cancel operations, and any cancel intent defaults to canceling all pending orders rather than a specific order.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust the 妙想 API key and environment configuration. Keep MX_API_URL set to the documented HTTPS service, use a limited or revocable API key if possible, and do not let the agent run buy, sell, or cancel requests unless you have clearly confirmed the exact action. Be aware that account and order responses are saved locally as raw JSON in the OpenClaw workspace.","findings":"[TT3] unexpected: Authenticated API calls are expected, but using an unrestricted environment-supplied base URL for key-bearing requests is broader than needed for the documented default service.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Trading and cancellation are advertised, but immediate execution without confirmation is a material concern; the implementation also maps any cancel request to cancel-all.\n[LP3] unexpected: The artifact does not define clear host, tool, or file-scope boundaries despite using secrets, outbound network calls, local writes, and account-changing actions.\n[E1] expected: The documented external POST requests are part of the simulated trading integration, so they are not exfiltration by themselves; the concern is the missing destination validation and action safeguards.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-only text is consistent with the China A-share and 妙想 service context and was not treated as a security escalation.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The advertised historical trade lookup appears to route to the general orders endpoint, which is a functionality mismatch but not a primary security concern.\n[SC1] expected: The requests dependency is expected for HTTP API access, but the unpinned requirement leaves a low supply-chain reproducibility gap.\n[SC4] expected: The advisory risk follows from the unpinned requests dependency; no malicious dependency source was present in the artifact.\n[T09] unexpected: Static scan concerns about unrestricted API destination and automatic account-data persistence are supported by the script and contribute to the Review verdict.\n[T08] expected: The dependency choice is ordinary for this purpose, but pinning and integrity controls are missing.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789192726278}}}}}